<HelpTab>
    <FluentText>
        <a href="/manage/feedback">Lanyard Feedback</a> collects what staff at every company say about Lanyard. It
        holds the thumbs up or down people send from the feedback button in the top bar, and the 1 to 5 star
        ratings from the occasional "How would you rate Lanyard?" prompt. Only platform admins can open it, and
        each one is also emailed to platform admins as it arrives.
    </FluentText>

    <HelpSection Title="Finding feedback">
        <FluentText>
            Use <strong>All</strong>, <strong>Good</strong>, <strong>Not great</strong> and <strong>Star ratings</strong>
            to choose which feedback to show, and turn on <strong>Unreviewed only</strong> to see just what's waiting.
            Each card shows the rating, the comment (if they left one), who sent it, their company and location, when,
            and the page they were on.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Dealing with feedback">
        <ol>
            <li>Read the card. Feedback you haven't reviewed yet has a <FluentBadge Appearance="BadgeAppearance.Tint" Color="BadgeColor.Brand">New</FluentBadge> badge.</li>
            <li>Select <strong>Reply</strong> to email the person from your own mail app. It only shows when they have an email address.</li>
            <li>Select <strong>Mark reviewed</strong> once it's dealt with. <strong>Mark unreviewed</strong> puts it back.</li>
        </ol>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
